BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uYwdRH4UKf7p6XYm7Hy9e
SUMMARY:Thalamo-cortical evoked effective connectivity to guide personalize
	d neuromodulation in epilepsy
DTSTAMP:20260730T054413Z
DTSTART:20260807T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:&#160\;  Speaker: Jasper Wang  Masters Candidate  Thesis Defens
	e  Department: Electrical and Computer Engineering  Location: BioScience R
	esearch Collaborative 875  Thalamic deep brain stimulation (DBS) has emerg
	ed as a promising treatment for drug-resistant epilepsy. Besides the anter
	ior nucleus of the thalamus (ANT)\, the only FDA-approved target\, the cen
	tromedian nucleus (CM) and pulvinar have also been shown to be promising t
	argets. However\, outcomes vary both across and within stimulation targets
	\, and to date there is no consensus on the optimal stimulation site withi
	n each thalamic nucleus. Here\, we hypothesized that effective connectivit
	y\, as quantified by thalamo-cortical evoked potentials (TCEPs)\, could gu
	ide personalized DBS target selection. We recorded scalp EEG responses to 
	single-pulse electrical stimulation delivered via thalamic DBS electrodes 
	in 15 epilepsy patients. Voxel-based linear mixed-effects modeling was app
	lied to TCEP data to generate stimulation-response maps with high spatiote
	mporal resolution. We provided group-level TCEP stimulation-response maps 
	of the CM and pulvinar\, and showed that pulvinar and CM subregions select
	ively engage distinct cortical networks\, detectable with non-invasive sca
	lp EEG. The pulvinar showed a medial-to-lateral gradient: medial pulvinar 
	mapped to anterior temporal cortex\, middle pulvinar to mid-temporal corte
	x\, and lateral pulvinar to parietal and posterior temporal cortex. Latera
	l-dorsal CM showed strong connectivity to frontocentral regions. Finally\,
	 we demonstrated a significant correlation between acute TCEP response and
	 long-term seizure reduction rate within the same patient cohort\, support
	ing the clinical translational potential of this approach.  &#160\;  Zoom 
	link: https://www.google.com/url?q=https://riceuniversity.zoom.us/j/936956
	67394?pwd%3DBlRXICqUVKI2MZvD1W2ySZwFarWfq1.1&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calenda
	r&amp\;ust=1785182094516539&amp\;usg=AOvVaw321gy5b1gZlvJrgy-BIX9J  (Depart
	ment : Electrical and Computer Engineering)\n\nhttps://events.rice.edu/eve
	nt/435445-thalamo-cortical-evoked-effective-connectivity-to\n\nFrom Rice U
	niversity - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/event/435445-thalamo-cortical-evoked-effective-
	connectivity-to
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
LOCATION:BioScience Research Collaborative
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:rice-public-events
CATEGORIES:Rice University - Open to the Public
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
