BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:wjv6JOSBB_0rjt6YHsleb
SUMMARY:Intoxication in British Literature\, 1660-1760
DTSTAMP:20260730T054413Z
DTSTART:20260810T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:&#160\;  Speaker: Rowan Morar  Doctoral Candidate  Thesis Defen
	se  Department: English  "Intoxication in British Literature\, 1660-1760" 
	argues for reading literary representations of intoxicants and altered sta
	tes of mind\, as a normative condition of Enlightenment life and a feature
	 of literary representation itself. Drawing from social history\, I trace 
	how mass markets for drugs\, such as plantation produced tobacco and spiri
	ts\, as well as opium left their imprints on the works of key authors of B
	ritish literary history—Lord Rochester\, Aphra Behn\, Daniel Defoe\, and C
	harlotte Lennox. I argue that these writers from 1660-1760\, the Restorati
	on to the mid-Enlightenment period\, represented the influx of colonially 
	produced drugs that became fiscal necessities for statecraft in order to m
	ake tacit assumptions about everyday self-regulation\, socialization\, and
	 politics visible. Profane appetites were as fundamentally changed in Brit
	ain as they were central to concepts of subjectivity in the violent coloni
	al theaters producing the intoxicants for an era of taste and refinement. 
	The construction of a subjective experience of intoxication in poems\, the
	 performance of drunkenness on the stage\, the narrative accounts of inner
	 consciousness affected by rum or tobacco\, wine or opium—all offer means 
	for seeing double: the work of intoxicants on literature and literary into
	xication during an increasingly global era of mass intoxication.  &#160\; 
	 https://riceuniversity.zoom.us/s/92686072682  (Department : English)\n\nh
	ttps://events.rice.edu/live/events/435789-intoxication-in-british-literatu
	re-1660-1760\n\nFrom Rice University - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/live/events/435789-intoxication-in-british-lite
	rature-1660-1760
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:rice-public-events
CATEGORIES:Rice University - Open to the Public
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:OIctapsmLm5ydhaNM-phi
SUMMARY:An Apparatus for Quantum Simulation with Rydberg Atoms
DTSTAMP:20260730T054413Z
DTSTART:20260810T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:&#160\;  Speaker: Brent Kruzel  Doctoral Candidate  Thesis Defe
	nse  Department: Physics &amp\; Astronomy  Location: Brockman Hall for Phy
	sics 300  This thesis presents the design\, construction\, and characteriz
	ation of a new experimental platform for quantum simulation using ultracol
	d strontium-88 Rydberg atoms. The apparatus was developed to support futur
	e optical-tweezer based experiments that realize synthetic dimensions thro
	ugh coherent millimeter-wave coupling between neighboring Rydberg states w
	hile providing the optical access\, electric- and magnetic-field control\,
	 and state-sensitive detection required for precision measurements. A new 
	science chamber was designed and integrated with laser cooling\, selective
	 field ionization\, and charged-particle detection systems\, while electro
	magnetic simulations were used to optimize millimeter-wave delivery and fi
	eld uniformity. Experimental characterization of the completed apparatus i
	ncludes measurements of static electric-field compensation\, millimeter-wa
	ve polarization purity\, and coherent Rydberg spectroscopy through Rabi an
	d Ramsey techniques. In addition\, analysis methods were developed to extr
	act relative Rydberg-state populations from selective field ionization sig
	nals\, and new high-precision microwave spectroscopy measurements were inc
	orporated into an updated determination of the quantum defect Rydberg-Ritz
	 parameters for the singlet S\, P\, and D Rydberg series of strontium. Tog
	ether\, these developments establish the experimental and analytical found
	ation for future quantum simulation experiments on this new apparatus.  &#
	160\;  (Department : Physics &amp\; Astronomy)\n\nhttps://events.rice.edu/
	event/435606-an-apparatus-for-quantum-simulation-with-rydberg\n\nFrom Rice
	 University - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/event/435606-an-apparatus-for-quantum-simulatio
	n-with-rydberg
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
LOCATION:Brockman Hall for Physics
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:rice-public-events
CATEGORIES:Rice University - Open to the Public
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
